  { // callseq 9 ... st.param.b64 [param0+0], %rd5; ... _bpf_helper_ext_0001 ... ld.param.b64 %rd9, [retval0+0]; } // callseq 9
A comment gives the same misread when the real def is the only one:
  // mov.u64 %rd5, 7;
  mov.u64 %rd5, 4;
The second works because constant_fd (lines 545-551) regex-searches the raw body, comments included, and takes the first match. In the first case std::stoll reads "010" in base 10.

  { // callseq 9 ... ld.param.b64 %rd15, [retval0+0]; } // callseq 9
