Exit: ld.u32 %rd17, [%rd15]; then %rd17 is used as data (e.g. an atomic add operand or key on a sum map).
The st32 branch accepts other == hit; the 'two lookup results' check only rejects different registers.

A (writing function):
	.loc 1 5 3
	ret;
$L__BB0_2: ret;
pieces() glues the first ret to .loc, so split_op gives `.loc` and it is not counted (955), while is_ret_line counts that line (1020). The labelled ret is counted by pieces but not by is_ret_line. The counts are 1 == 1, so the plan passes.
B (accesses):
$L__BB0_7: st.u32 [%rd9], %rd14;
/*
st.u32 [%rd9], %rd14;
*/
access_lines {s:1} comes from the real labelled store and on_lines {s:1} from the commented line (1024), so the plan passes.
Also `st.u32 [%rd9], %rd14; /*` on one line: line_statement strips the unterminated `/*` and the rewrite (1057-1058) drops it.

Map 10 is thread-local (in descs); map 8 is an ordinary array.
  mov.u64 %rd5, 010;   // PTX octal literal = 8 (PTX ISA 4.5.1)
  {callseq ... st.param.b64 [param0+0], %rd5; ... _bpf_helper_ext_0001 ... ld.param.b64 %rd9, [retval0+0];}
