Input: the lat_mmvq __probe_func__ from llvmbpf (registers as in dumpN70-lat_mmvq lines ~2560-2570), with one line added after the mov:
```
	mov.u64 	%SPL, __local_depot0;
	cvta.local.u64 	%SP, %SPL;
	add.u64 	%rd9, %SP, 0;
	add.u64 	%rd1, %SPL, 0;
	mov.u32 	%r4, 0;
	redux.sync.add.u32 	%r4, %r7, 0xffffffff;   // or: stacksave.u32 %r4;
	st.local.u32 	[%rd1+508], %r4;
	add.s64 	%rd10, %rd9, 508;
	mov.u64 	%rd11, 4;
	{ // callseq N, 0
	... st.param.b64 [param0+0], %rd11; ... st.param.b64 [param1+0], %rd10; ... call.uni (retval0), _bpf_helper_ext_0001, ...;
	ld.param.b64 	%rd15, [retval0+0];
	} // callseq N
	setp.eq.s64 %p1, %rd15, 0; ... ld.u32 %rd17, [%rd15]; ld.u32 %rd18, [%rd15+4];
```
Map 4 is thread-local with max_entries 1 and value_size 8, as in lat.

Trace:
- split_op (210-219) reads the mnemonic as "redux.sync.add.u32" (or "stacksave.u32"). build_index line 294, `op.rfind("st",0)==0 || op.rfind("red",0)==0 ... continue`, skips the statement before registers_in runs, so %r4 is not counted for it.
- forwarded_key (426-504): has_frame holds, and stack_slot(%rd10) gives %SP+508. Walking back from the call it passes mov and add, then reaches `st.local.u32 [%rd1+508], %r4`: the slot matches, the base is %SPL with .local, and count_defs(after,"%r4")==0, so it returns "%r4" with width 32. The redux comes before the store and is never examined.
- constant_key (843-856): count_defs(fbody,"%r4",&def)==1 with def="mov.u32 \t%r4, 0", which matches `^mov\.[ubs](?:32|64)\s+(%[\w$]+)\s*,\s*(0|[1-9]\d{0,9})$`, so key is 0.
- plan_by_value (932-938): 0 < max_entries, so pointers[%rd15] = offset + 0. The use loop (951-1009) sees only statements naming %rd15; the redux names %r4 and %r7, so it is not checked.
- route_function_body (1157-1168) emits `mov.u64 %rd15, 1; // ... by value`. The real dumpTV-lat_mmvq shows the same output: line 2570 `mov.u64 %rd15, 1`, lines 2574-2575 `cvt.u64.u32 %rd17, %bptv_h0` / `%rd18, %bptv_h1`.
- Memory form for the same input (1180-1201): key_into gives `mov.u32 %bptl_k0, %r4`, then `setp.lt.u32 %bptl_p0, %bptl_k0, 1` and selp. A warp sum of 1 or more gives NULL, so the program takes $L__BB0_3. By value, it reads entry 0 instead.

